ged findings.","requiredRepairs":[],"report":"## Editorial Assessment â€” climate-and-conflict-collide-as-indigenous-leaders-press-the\n\n### Deterministic Standards\nThe automated reading returns `publishable: true`, `wordCount: 864`, `referenceCount: 2`, `findings: []`. The `gates_clear: false` flag in manuscript frontmatter is a production-pipeline artifact; per standing instructions, the deterministic standards reading governs, not historical gate state.\n\n---\n\n### Claim Audit Against Witnessed Evidence\n\n**ICT News / Grist source (July 16, 2026) â€” full text witnessed:**\n\n| Manuscript claim | Source passage | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|\n| \"hundreds of delegates attending the 19th annual session of the UN Expert Mechanism on the Rights of Indigenous Peoples\" | \"hundreds of Indigenous delegates gather in Geneva at the 19th annual gathering of that United Nations body\" | SUPPORTED |\n| \"adopted nearly two decades ago by over 100 countries\" | \"it's been nearly 20 years since more than 100 countries adopted the United Nations Declaration on the Rights of Indigenous Peoples\" | SUPPORTED |\n| \"record-breaking storms still batter Indigenous lands, drought still desiccates them, and seas continue to rise\" | \"battered by record-breaking storms, dessicated by drought, and vanishing under rising seas\" | SUPPORTED |\n| EMRIP described as \"one of three UN bodies focused exclusively on Indigenous peoples...composed of seven Indigenous experts, each representing a different region\" | \"EMRIP, one of three U.N. organizations focused exclusively on Indigenous peoples, is composed of seven Indigenous experts, each representing a different region\" | SUPPORTED |\n| Session agenda includes \"inadequate disaster relief, artificial intelligence, and resource extraction\" | verbatim match in source | SUPPORTED |\n| \"Indigenous peoples continue dying by the hundreds in wars and while defending their lands\" | verbatim match in source | SUPPORTED |\n| Dhamai quote: \"Climate change, militarization, extractivism, and legal marginalization reinforce one another\" | verbatim in source | SUPPORTED |\n| Dhamai attribution: \"Tripura from the Chittagong Hill Tracts in Bangladesh and a former chair of EMRIP\" | matches source exactly | SUPPORTED |\n| Toki described as \"MÄori and EMRIP's member representing the Pacific region\" | matches source exactly | SUPPORTED |\n| Toki quote: \"It's a lose-lose situation for Indigenous peoples on all fronts\" | verbatim in source | SUPPORTED |\n| Breathing Lands described as \"vast wetland ecosystem that forms part of the Ring of Fire mineral deposit\" | \"the vast wetland ecosystem known as the Breathing Lands. It is part of the Ring of Fire mineral deposit\" | SUPPORTED |\n| \"strong resistance from Nishnawbe Aski Nation, which represents 49 First Nations communities\" | \"strong resistance from First Nations in the area, including the Nishnawbe Aski Nation, that represents 49 communities\" | SUPPORTED â€” manuscript adds \"First Nations\" as a clarifying descriptor, consistent with the surrounding source context; not a factual extension |\n| Mattinas co-founded Okiniwak in 2025 \"in response to Canadian legislation that allows projects to be advanced through an accelerated process\" | \"a youth organization created in 2025 in response to Canadian legislation that allows projects to be 'advanced through an accelerated process'\" | SUPPORTED |\n| \"the central question facing delegates remains the same as it was in 2007: not whether Indigenous rights should be recognized, but whether governments are prepared to uphold them\" | \"the central question facing delegates remains remarkably similar to the one asked in 2007: not whether Indigenous rights should be recognized, but whether governments are prepared to uphold them\" | SUPPORTED |\n\n**Cultural Survival source (July 13, 2026) â€” full text witnessed:**\n\n| Manuscript claim | Source passage | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|\n| Nepal's new government \"designated the Kathmandu-Tarai Fast Track expressway a top national priority\" | \"designated the multi-billion-dollar Kathmandu-Tarai Fast Track (expressway) as one of its top national infrastructure priorities\" | SUPPORTED |\n| Communities demand removal of \"army camps installed on their land without that consent\" | source describes army installing camps \"without the Free, Prior, and Informed Consent of the Indigenous Newar community\" | SUPPORTED |\n| Alternative route \"that the National Indigenous Nationalities Commission, Lalitpur Metropolitan City, and the Department of Archaeology have each formally recommended\" | all three bodies documented with specific letters or studies | SUPPORTED |\n\n**Unused sources (sources 3 and 4):** Both Cultural Survival items (Youth Fellows cohort; Bahia communicators meeting) are not cited and their summaries contain no usable content relevant to the manuscript's scope. Correctly excluded.\n\n---\n\n### Headline and Lede Faithfulness\n\nHeadline: *\"Climate and Conflict Collide as Indigenous Leaders Press the UN on Land Rights\"* â€” echoes the ICT News/Grist title without over-claiming. Does not convert the source's \"confront overlapping crises\" framing into a stronger factual commitment than the evidence supports. The lede is a direct, accurate summary of the EMRIP 19th session event and the convergent-threat framing. No mismatch between headline, lede, and body.\n\n---\n\n### Attribution Visibility\n\nBoth references are cited inline by name and hyperlink at every substantive use. No claims are presented as newsroom-originated facts; all are attributed to the named source publications. The ICT News / Grist dual attribution is appropriate given the publication chain described in the source (\"originally published by Grist...published through the Indigenous News Alliance\").\n\n---\n\n### Prose Assessment\n\nThe manuscript is specific throughout: named individuals with full identity context, named institutions, named geographic sites, named legislation, named dates. No confident abstraction unsupported by evidence. The three-section structure (UNDRIP gap â†’ convergent threats â†’ what leaders are demanding) is logical and avoids repetition. The Nepal paragraph functions correctly as a concrete grounding case rather than a tangential detour. Word count (864) is consistent with the deterministic reading.\n\n---\n\n### Pipeline Diagnosis\n\nNo failure layer identified. The writer model worked with two richly evidenced sources and produced clean, attributed, faithful prose. The `referenceCount: 2` matches the manuscript's reference block exactly. The assignment packet provided sufficient material to support the piece's scope.\n\n**Disposition: ACCEPT.**"}ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;HcEVbyWfwZXk1oqzkODQ70df5EfKUaShTod7fdyNFhMƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx9ni:///sha-256;ra74a-dVNodVoxUND6kohEXNJM604xEHQkTVvJf3sWMƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;grK6Sbz0P3Zc4aj8HoWthSMLwNiP7YnIyS4xj5bZ-AIƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;1qmSBaR0RjZc4JlS4AVolZh4f4PbNCKm6U7_p0jdscUƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkxclaude-code-cli-invocationsƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;eeVeizurGAjEvv-lNNgnOcRO-QVADlrHv9r8Tnlw9fwƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarka1ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;EvStHYWCdwsovGc4zHCZfIIVKAHy0qM3WeuADKjf1Ucƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarke84.93ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;L29LjO3-elGG1A9ZbIIcUwPHOoRlz61fJ-e3JmuTSGMƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dm